From: DHB_AX local port <local@invalid>
Subject: [LOCAL ONLY] ARM: mm: add HiSilicon L2 Cache V200 driver

The Hi3531 carries a 256 KB unified outer cache that no mainline driver
binds to.  It is a HiSilicon "L2 Cache V200", not an ARM PL310: the register
layouts do not overlap, and PL310's control register offset is this block's
auxiliary control register.  The vendor 3.0.8 SDK ships a working driver for
it, and this is that driver adapted to device-tree probing and current
outer-cache conventions.

Initialisation follows the uniphier outer cache: a single call at the end of
init_IRQ(), after irqchip_init() and before any DMA, with no machine
descriptor involved.  The board keeps matching __mach_desc_GENERIC_DT.

Several vendor behaviours are corrected rather than carried over.  Disabling
cleans and invalidates first, as outer_disable() requires.  Interrupt status
is cleared by writing back what L2_RINT reads, which is how every vendor
maintenance path clears AUTO_END; the vendor handler's write of zero would
clear nothing.  Range invalidation cleans partial boundary lines before
invalidating them, so an unaligned DMA buffer cannot discard dirty bytes of an
adjacent object, and every range operation ends in a sync inside the lock.
The lock is a raw spinlock because outer-cache operations run from atomic
context.

The shared-attribute override is set.  Section 3.11.2 of the datasheet states
that shared accesses are cacheable but do not allocate, and an SMP kernel maps
kernel and user memory as Shared, so without the override most of what the
board runs would never populate the cache.

Error reporting is deferred: the three interrupt lines stay masked and no
handler is registered.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/include/asm/hardware/cache-hil2v200.h b/arch/arm/include/asm/hardware/cache-hil2v200.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/include/asm/hardware/cache-hil2v200.h
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only */
+/*
+ * HiSilicon L2 Cache V200 outer cache controller.
+ */
+
+#ifndef __CACHE_HIL2V200_H
+#define __CACHE_HIL2V200_H
+
+#include <linux/errno.h>
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_CACHE_HIL2V200
+int hil2v200_cache_init(void);
+#else
+static inline int hil2v200_cache_init(void)
+{
+	return -ENODEV;
+}
+#endif
+
+#endif /* __CACHE_HIL2V200_H */
